   "evidence": "Basic.lean:839 `span : \u2200 v : V, \u2203 (a b : \u211d) (u : V), g K.q u = 0 \u2227 g (pTransverse g K) u = 0 \u2227 v = a \u2022 pTransverse g K + b \u2022 K.q + u` is the literal statement the new proof establishes with `a = g K.q v / g K.q K.q`, `b = g T v / g T T`; grep of `^(lemma|theorem|def|private ...)` over Basic.lean shows no existing standalone splitting lemma, and the only witness of `span` is the hand-built `spectatorAssumptions_kWit` at line 1096.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/QFT/Scattering/DIS/Tensors/Basic.lean",
   "fix": "Extract the splitting as a standalone public lemma in the same section, e.g. `exists_orthogonal_spectator (g) (K) (hSymm) (hqq : g K.q K.q \u2260 0) (hTT : g (pTransverse g K) (pTransverse g K) \u2260 0) (v) : \u2203 (a b : \u211d) (u : V), g K.q u = 0 \u2227 g (pTransverse g K) u = 0 \u2227 v = a \u2022 pTransverse g K + b \u2022 K.q + u`, and have `exists_apply_self_eq_of_isF1F2Decomposition` consume it.",
   "issue": "`exists_apply_self_eq_of_isF1F2Decomposition` builds the `q`/`p_T`-orthogonal splitting `v = a \u2022 q + b \u2022 T + u` inside its proof (`refine \u27e8v - a \u2022 K.q - b \u2022 T, ?_, ?_, ?_\u27e9`) and only returns the `W v v` value. The splitting mentions no `W` and no `IsF1F2Decomposition`; it is exactly the content posited by the `SpectatorAssumptions.span` field at line 839, which the same file still advertises as a hypothesis users must supply.",
   "line": 696
  }
